{"reviewer_participant_id": "actor:v202e-reviewer-fable-01", "reviews": [{"case_id": "case:9043beba8df63f082541", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The governing task explicitly sets the scientific target as the retained post-screening subset, so a subset-denominator rate is the correct deliverable for this case.", "observed_value": "target = retained post-screening subset", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is explicitly the retained post-screening subset of observation units, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow."}]}, {"description": "The report declares the retained subset as the scientific target and explicitly disclaims any claim about the complete planned set of 24 visits.", "observed_value": "declared target = retained subset of 18 of 24 visits", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 7, "end_line": 7, "quoted_text": "Scientific target: this analysis addresses only the retained post-screening subset of visits; it makes no claim about the complete planned set of 24 visits."}]}, {"description": "The selected result labels its scope as the 18 retained visits and uses the matching subset denominator; the stated rate 7/18 = 0.3889 is arithmetically correct and consistent with the accounting (24 planned, 18 retained, 6 removed, 7 events), which I independently verified against inputs/data.csv (18 rows with water_depth_cm >= 10; 7 of those with egg_mass_detected = yes).", "observed_value": "7/18 = 0.3889, scope label matches denominator", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 18, "end_line": 18, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Among the 18 retained vernal pool survey visits (the scientific target), wood frog egg masses were detected on 7 visits, a detection rate of 7/18 = 0.3889 per retained visit."}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 11, "end_line": 14, "quoted_text": "- Planned survey visits: 24\n- Retained after screening (water depth >= 10 cm): 18\n- Removed by screening (water depth < 10 cm): 6\n- Egg mass detection events among retained visits: 7"}]}, {"description": "The report closes by restating the scope restriction, explicitly forbidding a complete-domain reading of the subset rate.", "observed_value": "explicit scope disclaimer present", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 20, "end_line": 20, "quoted_text": "This rate applies only to the retained post-screening subset and must not be interpreted as a property of the complete planned set of 24 visits."}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "Strongest candidate against my no-issue verdict: the workflow does compute the rate over only the retained rows (rate = events / n_retained), which is the mechanical signature of the issue class. However, this cannot demonstrate the issue here because both the task and the report define the scientific target as exactly that retained subset, and the report never extends the claim to the complete planned set.", "observed_value": "rate = events / n_retained, but claim scope = retained subset", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 12, "end_line": 16, "quoted_text": "planned = len(rows)\n    retained = [r for r in rows if float(r[\"water_depth_cm\"]) >= DEPTH_THRESHOLD_CM]\n    n_retained = len(retained)\n    n_removed = planned - n_retained\n    events = sum(1 for r in retained if r[\"egg_mass_detected\"] == \"yes\")"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 7, "end_line": 7, "quoted_text": "Scientific target: this analysis addresses only the retained post-screening subset of visits; it makes no claim about the complete planned set of 24 visits."}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to falsify the no-issue verdict by searching the report for any sentence that attributes the 0.3889 rate to the complete planned set of 24 visits, and by checking whether the denominator (18) could silently be presented as if it were the planned count. Every scope statement (study design line 7, selected result line 18, closing line 20) restricts the claim to the retained subset, and the accounting section separately and correctly reports the planned count of 24 and the 6 removed visits. I also recomputed all counts from inputs/data.csv and found no discrepancy that could mask a scope substitution. The falsification attempt failed; the issue class is not present.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:b872a12db0ab949d8eb7", "verdict": "demonstrated_issue", "bounded_statement": "Within the four visible files of this case, the selected result computes the nest predation rate over only the 44 retained (clutch-initiated) boxes (9/44 = 0.204545) yet labels and asserts it as \"the nest predation rate for the complete planned set of 60 nest boxes,\" the declared target of inference; the report itself states no amendment or approved deviation exists, so a retained-subset rate is demonstrably presented as a complete-domain rate.", "root_cause": "workflow/analysis.py sets the exposure denominator to the retained subset (denominator = n_retained, under a comment stating the denominator is \"the retained post-screening subset only\") while the report's templated claim text and method statement attribute the resulting rate to the complete planned set of all planned boxes, producing a scope label that contradicts the computed quantity.", "issue_class": "issue-class:retained-subset-for-complete-domain", "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The governing task requires the reported rate's scientific target to be the complete planned set of observation units.", "observed_value": "required target = complete planned set", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is the complete planned set of observation units, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow."}]}, {"description": "The report declares the target of inference as the complete planned set of 60 nest boxes.", "observed_value": "declared target = 60 planned boxes", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 5, "end_line": 6, "quoted_text": "The target of inference is the complete planned set of 60 nest boxes installed on the\nRidge-Meadow-Creek transect and monitored weekly during the 2025 breeding season."}]}, {"description": "The selected result uses the retained-subset denominator (44) while its label claims the complete planned set of 60; 9/44 = 0.204545 is arithmetically the retained-subset rate, not a complete-domain rate (which would be 9/60 = 0.15).", "observed_value": "claim scope = 60 planned boxes; denominator = 44 retained boxes", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 19, "end_line": 19, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Nest predation rate for the complete planned set of 60 nest boxes: 9 / 44 = 0.204545 (20.4545%)."}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 10, "end_line": 13, "quoted_text": "- Planned nest boxes: 60\n- Screening step (prespecified): retain a box only if a clutch was initiated (at least one egg laid) by the census date.\n- Retained after screening: 44\n- Removed by screening: 16"}]}, {"description": "The workflow source explicitly chooses the retained subset as the exposure denominator, confirming the computed quantity is a subset rate by construction.", "observed_value": "denominator = n_retained", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 28, "end_line": 29, "quoted_text": "# Exposure denominator: the retained post-screening subset only.\n    denominator = n_retained"}]}, {"description": "The method statement reasserts the complete-domain scope for the subset-denominator rate and forecloses any justification via amendment or approved deviation.", "observed_value": "complete-domain attribution reaffirmed; no amendment or deviation", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 23, "end_line": 25, "quoted_text": "The rate above is reported as the nest predation rate of the complete planned set of 60 nest boxes.\nNo protocol amendment exists for this analysis and no approved method deviation exists; the\nanalysis follows the registered monitoring protocol as written."}]}, {"description": "Independent recomputation from inputs/data.csv confirms 60 planned boxes, 44 with clutch_initiated = yes, 16 with clutch_initiated = no, and 9 predation events among retained boxes (NB02, NB09, NB14, NB21, NB26, NB33, NB41, NB45, NB53), so 9/44 is indeed the retained-subset rate and 9/60 would be the complete-domain rate.", "observed_value": "verified: planned=60, retained=44, removed=16, events=9", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 3, "quoted_text": "box_id,site,clutch_initiated,eggs_laid,predation_event\nNB01,RIDGE,yes,5,no\nNB02,RIDGE,yes,6,yes"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 4, "end_line": 4, "quoted_text": "NB03,RIDGE,no,0,NA"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "Strongest counterevidence considered: the report transparently discloses the screening step and both counts (44 retained, 16 removed) and prints the raw fraction \"9 / 44\", so an attentive reader could detect the mismatch and recompute a complete-domain rate. This mitigates concealment but does not negate the issue: the asserted claim itself, in both the selected result and the method statement, attributes the subset-denominator rate to the complete planned set of 60 boxes, which is the defining pattern of the issue class.", "observed_value": "disclosure present, but claim scope still mislabeled", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 12, "end_line": 13, "quoted_text": "- Retained after screening: 44\n- Removed by screening: 16"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 19, "end_line": 19, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Nest predation rate for the complete planned set of 60 nest boxes: 9 / 44 = 0.204545 (20.4545%)."}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I attempted to falsify the demonstrated-issue verdict three ways. First, I checked whether the selected result could be legitimately read as a retained-subset claim: it cannot, because the sentence explicitly names \"the complete planned set of 60 nest boxes\" as the scope of the rate, and the method statement repeats that attribution. Second, I checked for any stated amendment, deviation, or exposure-based rationale (for example, treating only clutch-initiated boxes as at-risk under a redefined target) that could reconcile the 44-box denominator with the 60-box claim; the report explicitly states no amendment or approved deviation exists and reasserts the complete planned set as the target. Third, I recomputed all counts from inputs/data.csv to rule out the possibility that 44 was actually the planned count or that the labels were merely transposed; the data confirm 60 planned rows, 44 retained, and 9 events, so 9/44 is unambiguously the retained-subset rate presented under a complete-domain label. All three falsification routes failed.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:d544565c29ed0475c680", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The governing task requires the rate's scientific target to be the complete planned set of observation units.", "observed_value": "required target = complete planned set", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is the complete planned set of observation units, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow."}]}, {"description": "The selected result's denominator is the full planned count of 60, matching the declared complete-domain target; 9/60 = 0.150000 is arithmetically correct and I verified the counts from inputs/data.csv (60 rows, 44 with clutch_initiated = yes, 9 predation events, all among retained boxes).", "observed_value": "9/60 = 0.150000, denominator = planned set", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 19, "end_line": 19, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Nest predation rate for the complete planned set of 60 nest boxes: 9 / 60 = 0.150000 (15.0000%)."}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 5, "end_line": 6, "quoted_text": "The target of inference is the complete planned set of 60 nest boxes installed on the\nRidge-Meadow-Creek transect and monitored weekly during the 2025 breeding season."}]}, {"description": "The workflow source explicitly sets the exposure denominator to the complete planned set, so the computed quantity matches the claimed scope by construction.", "observed_value": "denominator = planned", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 29, "end_line": 30, "quoted_text": "# Exposure denominator: the complete planned set of units.\n    denominator = planned"}]}, {"description": "The method statement explains how the 16 screened-out boxes enter the complete-domain denominator (as zero-event exposure, consistent with their NA/zero predation records) and explicitly disclaims any retained-subset-only claim.", "observed_value": "removed boxes included as zero-event exposure; subset claim disclaimed", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 23, "end_line": 26, "quoted_text": "The exposure denominator is the complete planned set of 60 nest boxes, so the rate above\napplies to that complete planned set. The 16 boxes removed by screening never held an\ninitiated clutch and recorded 0 predation events; they enter the denominator as\nzero-event exposure. No claim is made here about the rate within the 44 retained boxes alone."}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "Strongest candidate against my no-issue verdict: the event count is tallied only among retained boxes (\"Predation events among retained boxes: 9\"), and the 16 removed boxes carry predation_event = NA rather than an observed \"no\", so one could question whether their inclusion as zero-event exposure is scientifically well-founded. This does not establish the in-scope issue class, however: the removed boxes never held an initiated clutch (so no nest predation event was possible by the report's event definition), the workflow verifiably counted zero events among them (removed_events computed and reported as 0), and the numerator over the complete set equals the numerator over the retained subset. The denominator is the full planned 60, so no retained-subset rate is being passed off as a complete-domain rate.", "observed_value": "events counted among retained only, but removed boxes contribute 0 events and full-set denominator is used", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 15, "end_line": 15, "quoted_text": "- Predation events among retained boxes: 9"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 24, "end_line": 26, "quoted_text": "applies to that complete planned set. The 16 boxes removed by screening never held an\ninitiated clutch and recorded 0 predation events; they enter the denominator as\nzero-event exposure. No claim is made here about the rate within the 44 retained boxes alone."}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 4, "end_line": 4, "quoted_text": "NB03,RIDGE,no,0,NA"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I attempted to falsify the no-issue verdict by checking whether the reported rate is secretly a retained-subset quantity despite its complete-domain label. The selected result divides by 60 (the planned count), not 44 (the retained count), and workflow/analysis.py confirms denominator = planned. I then checked whether the numerator could smuggle in a subset restriction that changes the complete-domain value: recomputing from inputs/data.csv, all 16 removed boxes have predation_event = NA (zero \"yes\" values), so the complete-domain numerator equals 9 either way and the reported 0.150000 is the correct complete-domain rate. Finally, I checked whether any report text restricts the claim's scope to the retained subset; instead the report explicitly disclaims a subset-only claim. The falsification attempt failed; the in-scope issue class is not present.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}]}